{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>נשא עון ופשע.</b> An expression of נשיאת פנים (showing partiality), דפורטנ״ט in the foreign tongue — He shows partiality to the penitent." "<b>ונקה לא ינקה.</b> Altogether, if they do not improve their deeds." "<b>פקד עון אבות.</b> For a burden too heavy for one is manageable for two, and what is heavy for two is manageable for three. For if a person were punished in full for his sin, the world could not endure. Rather, he is punished in part and his offspring are punished in part — and this is the attribute of the thirteen, which is also for the good. And as for what is written ״fathers shall not be put to death for children״ — that is in a human court, while here is in the heavenly court." "<b>[על שלשים ועל רבעים.</b> Such is the way of HaShem to exact retribution from a person in the fourth generation — as it is written, ״upon the third and upon the fourth,״ that is, upon the third a little, and upon the fourth everything — to extirpate them from the world.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:48.617861710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}